Title: Consecutive Character Fix Demo
Author: Test Suite
Draft date: 2024-12-01

FADE IN:

INT. TEST ROOM - DAY

This test demonstrates the fix for consecutive character dialogue parsing.
Before the fix, all the following characters would be parsed as a single dialogue block.
After the fix, each character should get their own dialogue_block.

                    ALICE
          I'm the first character to speak.

                    BOB
          I'm the second character, right after Alice.

                    CHARLIE
          And I'm the third character in sequence.

                    ALICE
          Alice speaks again immediately.

                    BOB (O.S.)
          Bob responds from off-screen.

                    CHARLIE (V.O.)
          Charlie does voice-over.

@COMPUTER
System announcement.

                    ALICE
                    (surprised)
          Alice reacts to the computer.

                    BOB
                    (to Charlie)
          Bob addresses Charlie directly.

                    CHARLIE
                    (nodding)
          Charlie acknowledges.

~ALICE hums
La la la...

                    BOB
          Bob interrupts the humming.

This should result in separate dialogue_block nodes for each character,
with proper character highlighting for each name.

FADE OUT.

THE END
